      "description": "Square ruled input with a tracked narrow-caps label.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-field\"><span class=\"ds-field-label\">Title</span><input class=\"ds-input\" placeholder=\"Laptop will not boot\"></label>",
      "css": ".ds-field{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;max-width:320px}.ds-field-label{font:600 12px 'Archivo Narrow',Archivo,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#262a7a}.ds-input{font:400 15px Archivo,system-ui,sans-serif;height:36px;padding:0 12px;background:#fefefc;color:#1d1d22;border:1px solid rgba(38,42,122,.5);border-radius:0;caret-color:#262a7a}.ds-input::placeholder{color:#5f6185}.ds-input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #262a7a;outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Carbon Rail",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "nav-rail",
      "description": "232px carbon nav rail; the active item is a tab in the ground colour.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-rail\"><div class=\"ds-rail-sec\">Work</div><a class=\"ds-rail-link\" data-active>Incidents</a><a class=\"ds-rail-link\">Report incident</a><a class=\"ds-rail-link\">Profile</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-rail{width:232px;background:#262a7a;padding:8px 0}.ds-rail-sec{padding:16px 18px 6px;font:600 11px 'Archivo Narrow',Archivo,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#a9acdc}.ds-rail-link{display:block;padding:9px 18px;font:500 14px Archivo,sans-serif;color:#e6e7f6;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color 120ms ease-out}.ds-rail-link:hover{background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);color:#fff}.ds-rail-link[data-active]{background:#eef2f1;color:#262a7a;font-weight:700}.ds-rail-link:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #fff;outline-offset:-2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Top Bar with Role Tag and Live Chip",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "top-bar",
      "description": "Ground header with a 3px role-accent rule, filled role tag and green Live chip (technician shown).",
      "html": "<header class=\"ds-top\"><span class=\"ds-role\">Technician &middot; A. Rao</span><span class=\"ds-live\"><span class=\"ds-dot\"></span>Live</span></header>",
      "css": ".ds-top{height:56px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:0 16px;background:#f2eff1;border-top:3px solid #6a2c5b;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(38,42,122,.5)}.ds-role{font:600 12px 'Archivo Narrow',Archivo,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#fff;background:#6a2c5b;padding:5px 10px}.ds-live{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:4px 10px 4px 9px;font:700 12px 'Archivo Narrow',Archivo,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#157a3e;background:#e3f3e8;border:1px solid #157a3e}.ds-dot{position:relative;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#157a3e}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){.ds-dot::after{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid #157a3e;animation:ds-pulse 2s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) infinite}}@keyframes ds-pulse{from{transform:scale(1);opacity:.9}to{transform:scale(3.2);opacity:0}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Priority Stamps",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "priority-stamp",
      "description": "P1-P4 magnitude ramp in size and border weight; P1 is a red double rule.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-pri\" data-l=\"P1\">P1</span><span class=\"ds-pri\" data-l=\"P2\">P2</span><span class=\"ds-pri\">P3</span><span class=\"ds-pri\" data-l=\"P4\">P4</span>",
      "css": ".ds-pri{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;font:700 13px/1 'Courier Prime',monospace;color:#1d1d22;border:1px solid #1d1d22;padding:3px 6px;margin-right:6px}.ds-pri[data-l=P1]{color:#c8102e;border:3px double #c8102e;font-size:15px;padding:2px 6px}.ds-pri[data-l=P2]{border-width:2px;font-size:14px;padding:2px 6px}.ds-pri[data-l=P4]{border-style:dashed;color:#4d4f74;border-color:#4d4f74}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status and SLA Marks",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "status-mark",
      "description": "Ruled status caps (filled when active) and SLA line marks.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-st\">New</span><span class=\"ds-st\" data-on>In progress</span><span class=\"ds-st\" data-hold>On hold</span><span class=\"ds-sla\">On track</span><span class=\"ds-sla\" data-b>Breached</span>",
      "css": ".ds-st{display:inline-block;font:600 11px/1.3 'Archivo Narrow',Archivo,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#262a7a;border:1px solid #262a7a;padding:2px 7px;margin-right:6px}.ds-st[data-on]{background:#262a7a;color:#fefefc}.ds-st[data-hold]{border-style:dashed}.ds-sla{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font:400 13px Archivo,sans-serif;color:#1d1d22;margin-right:10px}.ds-sla::before{content:'';width:18px;border-top:2px solid #262a7a}.ds-sla[data-b]{color:#c8102e;font-weight:700;text-decoration:line-through;text-decoration-thickness:2px}.ds-sla[data-b]::before{border-top:4px double #c8102e}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lifecycle Stamp Strip",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "lifecycle-stamp",
      "description": "Signature: one tilted rubber stamp per lifecycle step; the current step is pressed in red.",
      "html": "<ol class=\"ds-strip\"><li class=\"ds-stamp\"><b>New</b><i>09:12</i></li><li class=\"ds-stamp\"><b>Assigned</b><i>09:20</i></li><li class=\"ds-stamp\" data-now><b>In progress</b><i>10:04</i></li><li class=\"ds-stamp\" data-todo><b>Resolved</b></li><li class=\"ds-stamp\" data-todo><b>Closed</b></li></ol>",
      "css": ".ds-strip{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:4px 2px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(112px,1fr));gap:10px}.ds-stamp{min-height:56px;border:1.5px solid #262a7a;color:#262a7a;display:grid;place-content:center;text-align:center;gap:2px;padding:6px 4px;transform:rotate(-1.5deg)}.ds-stamp:nth-child(2n){transform:rotate(1.2deg)}.ds-stamp b{font:700 11.5px 'Archivo Narrow',Archivo,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase}.ds-stamp i{font:700 13px 'Courier Prime',monospace;font-style:normal}.ds-stamp[data-todo]{border:1px dashed rgba(38,42,122,.5);color:#4d4f74;transform:none}.ds-stamp[data-now]{border:2.5px solid #c8102e;color:#c8102e;transform:rotate(-2.5deg)}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){.ds-stamp[data-now]{animation:ds-press 140ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)}}@keyframes ds-press{from{transform:rotate(-2.5deg) scale(1.08);opacity:.6}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Ruled Sheet",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "sheet",
      "description": "White sheet on the ground with a 1px carbon rule, square and flat; field cells divided by faint rules.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-sheet\"><div class=\"ds-cell\"><span class=\"ds-lab\">Category</span><div class=\"ds-val\">Hardware</div></div><div class=\"ds-cell\"><span class=\"ds-lab\">Assigned to</span><div class=\"ds-val\">A. Rao</div></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-sheet{background:#fefefc;border:1px solid rgba(38,42,122,.5);display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr));max-width:420px}.ds-cell{padding:12px 20px;border-right:1px solid rgba(38,42,122,.22)}.ds-lab{font:600 11px 'Archivo Narrow',Archivo,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#262a7a}.ds-val{font:500 15px Archivo,sans-serif;color:#1d1d22;margin-top:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "ASCII Name Banner",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Profile name drawn as a figlet Big banner in Courier Prime 400 carbon; real name visually hidden; non-ASCII names fall back to Archivo 800.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-ascii\"><span class=\"ds-sr\">Ada Lin</span><pre class=\"ds-art\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"--cols:39\">              _         _      _\n     /\\      | |       | |    (_)\n    /  \\   __| | __ _  | |     _ _ __\n   / /\\ \\ / _` |/ _` | | |    | | '_ \\\n  / ____ \\ (_| | (_| | | |____| | | | |\n /_/    \\_\\__,_|\\__,_| |______|_|_| |_|</pre></div>",
      "css": ".ds-ascii{container-type:inline-size;max-width:420px}.ds-art{margin:0;font-family:'Courier Prime','Courier New',monospace;font-weight:400;font-size:min(18px,calc(100cqw / (var(--cols) * .6)));line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:0;white-space:pre;color:#262a7a;overflow:hidden}.ds-sr{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Service Docket",
    "overview": "Every incident is a numbered docket from a carbon job book, and every lifecycle step leaves a dated rubber stamp on it. The interface is printed in one ink, carbon blue, on a quiet paper ground. White sheets are ruled in one-pixel carbon, corners are square, and nothing casts a shadow. Docket numbers, times and counts are typed in Courier Prime. Field labels are tracked narrow capitals, as on a pre-printed form. The system turns away from the stock SaaS admin look: default indigo, rounded cards, pill badges and shadowed panels.\n\nThe palette does the explaining. Carbon carries almost everything. Stamp red appears only when something is genuinely wrong (a P1 docket, a breached or at-risk SLA, the current or voided lifecycle stamp). The signed-in role shows as one muted accent: teal for employees, plum for technicians, bronze for administrators. That accent fills the header role tag, the 3px top rule and the avatar box, and the page ground carries only a faint hint of it. Green belongs to the real-time connection chip and nowhere else.\n\nThe density is operational. Tables are ruled straight onto the ground, and the row under the pointer or focus lifts to a white sheet. Urgency is shown in form as well as colour: stamp size, border weight and line style rank priority and SLA state, so meaning never depends on hue alone.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Carbon-blue ink and rail (#262a7a) on a near-neutral role-tinted ground.",
      "Square corners everywhere (radius 0). Flat colour, no shadows, no gradients.",
      "One-pixel carbon rules for sheets, tables and field boxes.",
      "Three type voices: Archivo for the interface, Archivo Narrow tracked caps for labels, Courier Prime for typed figures.",
      "A mark grammar of solid, double, dashed, dotted and struck lines for priority, status and SLA.",
      "A lifecycle stamp strip with slight alternating tilts, where the current step is pressed in red."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Four Inks Rule",
        "body": "Carbon, stamp red, the one active role accent and the Live chip's green are the only hues. The theme remaps Mantine's `green`, `teal` and `orange` to carbon so that defaults cannot add a fifth.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Real Alarm Rule",
        "body": "Stamp red marks only P1, SLA at risk or breached, the current, held or voided lifecycle stamp, and over capacity. A button, link or heading in red is a defect.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Rule",
        "body": "A screen shows the signed-in role's accent and no other role's accent. The accent identifies who you are. It never encodes priority, status or action.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Green Is Connection Rule",
        "body": "Green means the real-time connection is live. It is never used for success, \"met\" or \"available\".",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Typed Figure Rule",
        "body": "Docket numbers, times, priorities, counts and levels are set in Courier Prime. Table cells use tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Form Label Rule",
        "body": "Tracked narrow capitals label a field, column or state that sits directly next to its value. They are never used as a decorative line above a headline.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Paper Rule",
        "body": "Nothing casts a shadow and nothing uses a gradient. To separate a surface, change the paper (ground to sheet white) or rule it in 1px carbon.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep every corner at radius 0 and every shadow at `none`.",
      "**Do** rule sheets, tables and fields in 1px carbon-rule, and use carbon-rule-faint for internal dividers.",
      "**Do** encode priority and SLA in line form (size, weight, double, dashed, dotted, struck) as well as colour.",
      "**Do** set docket numbers, times, priorities and counts in Courier Prime 700 with tabular numerals.",
      "**Do** derive the role from `html[data-role]` and use only `--app-accent` for the role tag, the 3px top rule, the avatar and the user's own role card.",
      "**Do** lift the hovered or focused table row to sheet white rather than tinting it.",
      "**Do** tint secondary text from carbon (#4d4f74 light, #a8a9c4 dark) so it holds AA on every ground.",
      "**Do** gate every animation behind `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`.",
      "**Do** keep the real text available to assistive technology whenever a figure is drawn decoratively (the ASCII name banner is `aria-hidden` and has a visually hidden name)."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use stamp red for actions, links, headings or decoration. It is for P1, at-risk or breached SLA, and the current, held or voided stamp only.",
      "**Don't** use green anywhere except the Live connection chip. It never means success, met or available.",
      "**Don't** show another role's accent, or use a role accent to encode state.",
      "**Don't** introduce rounded cards, pill badges, shadowed panels, gradients or default Mantine indigo.",
      "**Don't** let Mantine colour defaults (`red`, `yellow`) render as raw hues. Map them to carbon or stamp.",
      "**Don't** put tracked narrow capitals above a headline as an eyebrow. Labels sit next to the value they name."
    ]
  }
}